From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:27:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09924/11362] Stamp the version that judged, not the one on
 disk; widen coverage

Adversarial review of dc8316b43d found the mechanism certified a stale
verdict as current -- the origin incident inverted. Four confirmed defects,
all fixed here.

1. WRONG VERSION STAMPED. make_provenance fingerprinted the gate source ON
   DISK, but the verdict comes from the LOADED module.
   _module_with_current_source() falls back to the cached module when a
   reload fails, so a half-landed edit paired an OLD verdict with a NEW
   version and reported it `current` -- worse than the legacy state, which
   at least reads `unversioned`. verify_artifact now returns the judging
   module's own LOADED_GATE_VERSION, computed at import, and both stampers
   use it.

2. COVERAGE MISSED THE DOMINANT CHECK. NONTERMINAL_DECLARED_ARTIFACT is 995
   of the corpus's 1,126 critical flags and is decided entirely by tables in
   carnot/terminal_artifacts.py. Commit 4a1557fd85 added "disqualified" to
   TERMINAL_CLASSES and flipped that verdict for real artifacts without
   touching adversarial_verify.py. The version now spans both files.

3. gate_version_algo was written and never read. A version from another
   algorithm now reads `unversioned` instead of being compared as if it
   were comparable.

4. backfill_stamps and conductor_gates read the determination with a bare
   .get, so a principle-wrapped {"value": false} read as truthy. Latent
   today (0 artifacts wrap it); fixed.

MEASURED LIMITS, now stated in the spec and the note rather than implied
away:
- `stale` saturates. Over 128 tracked gate revisions the AST normalization
  suppressed 1 version bump (0.8%), and the gate changed ~9x/day in the
  week to 2026-08-25. A fresh stamp reads `stale` within hours. `stale`
  means "the gate moved", not "this verdict would change". The durable
  value is the recorded version and timestamp.
- Coverage is source files, not data. ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml feeds a
  critical flag and is not fingerprinted.

NOTE CORRECTIONS, all re-derived independently:
- Direction B is NOT mostly fabrication. 773 of the 864 NONTERMINAL-only
  artifacts classify `unknown` -- old results with status success whose
  verdicts predate the Verdict Terminal-Prefix Discipline. Only ~91 are
  genuinely non-terminal. A default backfill would trade 200 stale false
  positives for ~773 fresh ones. The earlier framing is retracted in place.
- The printed commands reach fewer artifacts than quoted: the tool globs
  results/experiment_*.json, so --backfill is 1,054 and
  --high-precision-only is 4, not 1,090 and 21. Direction A is unaffected;
  all 565 stamped and all 200 clearing are inside the glob.
- "164 draw no flag at all" narrowed to "no critical and no warning flag".

An existing REQ-VERIFY-6593 test asserted the report dict exactly; it now
matches the delegation marker and asserts the version is carried. Intent
unchanged, assertion no longer over-specified.

Tests: 26, all passing. Mutation-proved 13/13 RED-on-delete,
GREEN-on-restore, in a git worktree with resolution verified by import.
Nothing under results/ was written.

